  "instance_name": "anti_black_stereotype_athletic_ability",
  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Athletic Ability as Sole Competency",
  "description": "A disparaging stereotype that reduces Black individuals to their physical abilities, implying they are only valued for their athleticism or physical appearance, and lack other competencies or intellectual depth. This stereotype is often used to dehumanize or marginalize Black people, particularly in contexts where their physicality is highlighted (e.g., fitness, sports).",
